- If the queue was non-empty (i.e., `this.size() > 0` in the old state),
- Then after the operation, the size is decreased by one: `this.size() == \old(this.size()) - 1`.

Using the `\old` syntax to refer to the state before the method call, and the implication operator `=>`, we can write this as:

<code>assert \old(this.size()) > 0 => this.size() == \old(this.size()) - 1;</code>
